  "intro": "Evergreen's NASCAR Championship Night, and the 68 keeps rolling. Bart Hecter Jr banked quick-time money, a heat, and the full 25 in the main — 78 points on the night — to push the championship lead to 557. But this is still a three-car fight: Quatsoe's 8 is 27 back at 530, and Cheth's 23 another 13 behind on 517. Vince Conwell holds fourth at 484 in the Northwest Concrete Cutting car, with Shane Strimple's 57 right on his bumper at 477 after a strong 72-point night.\n\nBryan Roundtree lit up the 10 for the best run of his season — 63 points, quick-time sharp. And a new number joined the show: S. Conduff unloaded the 31 for the first time and left with 53. One points race left — the Fall Classic at Tri-City. Points stay with the car, not the driver.",
